+// allocator pick them: TLSF rounds a request up to the next size class
+// before it searches (64 KB steps at this size), so a hole of exactly the
+// buffer's size would be passed over for the big free region behind it.
+// With the extra it sits in the class the search starts at, below the rest
+// of the heap, so both buffers land at the start of the two holes. The tail
